<title>TURKEY: Turkish c.bank reserves down $26 mln last week.</title>
<headline>Turkish c.bank reserves down $26 mln last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves fell by $26 million to $17.199 billion in the week to November 15.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollar</p>
<p>		   November 15    November 8   end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve   17.199	  17.225	 12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve     1.383	   1.383	  1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve   18.582	  18.608	 13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $96 million to $27.944 billion in the week ending November 1, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom, 90-212-275 0875. IMA EKS</p>
</text>
